      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:02 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners (Karen Howsam et al.)",
      "case_id": "2002-01-800",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "f89204d3508f9be4ac53da0dad126e0865db592ef9e61da87164826d393e6eab",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f89204d3508f-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There is at least a little irony in the fact that Dean Witter is the litigant here before you, about 27 years past the time when it started with Dean Witter and Byrd the -- the move toward closing the courthouse doors to public investors and forcing them into industry-run arbitration. Dean Witter is now back here attempting to place a hurdle in the way of the public investor who ironically at this point seeks to enforce an arbitration agreement."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent (Dean Witter Reynolds)",
      "case_id": "2002-01-800",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "f89204d3508f9be4ac53da0dad126e0865db592ef9e61da87164826d393e6eab",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f89204d3508f-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The respondents here, of course, argue that because of the not to be submitted clause, the 6 years, that limits the scope of the -- of the arbitration agreement."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2002-01-800",
      "confidence": 0.92,
      "document_hash": "f89204d3508f9be4ac53da0dad126e0865db592ef9e61da87164826d393e6eab",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f89204d3508f-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Well, so is 10324 which you're relying on. That is, the arbitrator shall be empowered to interrupt and determine the applicability of. I mean, that's -- MR. FRIEDBERG: Exactly, Justice Scalia."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (amicus curiae)",
      "case_id": "2002-01-800",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "f89204d3508f9be4ac53da0dad126e0865db592ef9e61da87164826d393e6eab",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f89204d3508f-0000-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "For two reasons the question whether petitioners' claims were submitted within the 6-year time limit is for the arbitrators to decide."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2002-01-800",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f89204d3508f9be4ac53da0dad126e0865db592ef9e61da87164826d393e6eab",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f89204d3508f-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: What is -- what is the general principle that Justice Ginsburg was asking for that controls your first conclusion?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Roberts",
      "case_id": "2002-01-800",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f89204d3508f9be4ac53da0dad126e0865db592ef9e61da87164826d393e6eab",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f89204d3508f-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Arbitrability is, as used in the Court's cases, a term of art that includes two questions. One of those questions is whether the parties are bound by a valid arbitration agreement and the other question is whether the subject matter of their underlying dispute is within the scope of that agreement."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Starr",
      "case_id": "2002-01-800",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f89204d3508f9be4ac53da0dad126e0865db592ef9e61da87164826d393e6eab",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f89204d3508f-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But eligible is a very familiar term. It is found in rule 6 of the Court, and what it means is if you're not eligible, you don't get to this podium. You don't go to the forum."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2002-01-800",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f89204d3508f9be4ac53da0dad126e0865db592ef9e61da87164826d393e6eab",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f89204d3508f-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: But you can agree to a temporal restriction and still not commit yourself as to who decides whether that restriction is true."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Starr",
      "case_id": "2002-01-800",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "f89204d3508f9be4ac53da0dad126e0865db592ef9e61da87164826d393e6eab",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f89204d3508f-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. STARR: Because she agreed in the submission agreement to be bound by arbitration under the code of procedure. It's an express agreement by her which she signed, which goes back to paragraph 19 --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice (unspecified)",
      "case_id": "2002-01-800",
      "confidence": 0.8,
      "document_hash": "f89204d3508f9be4ac53da0dad126e0865db592ef9e61da87164826d393e6eab",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f89204d3508f-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Well, so we're just talking here, when you say the NASD has said, this is incorporated in the code of procedure which she agreed to be bound by?"
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
